course: dictionary
lesson: 3500
title: Rude words and polite words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are rude. «Fart» is a rude, informal word, so you do not use it in polite talk, in class or with grown-ups you do not know well. You will still meet it in books and jokes, so it helps to know what it means and when it is used.
explain: Polite words for the same thing are «pass wind» and «break wind». «Toot» and «trump» are childish, joking words. Context tells you which kind of word you are reading: the speaker's tone, the setting and the other words around it.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Fart around» means to waste time doing silly things, and «an old fart» is a rude name for a boring or old-fashioned person. Look at the words around the word to see which meaning fits.
fact: «Fart» is a rude, informal word for letting gas out from the bottom.
fact: Most fart gas is made by bacteria in the large gut breaking down fibre from beans, vegetables and bread.
fact: Most fart gas has no smell at all; only a tiny bit of sulphur gas makes the stink.
fact: «Toot» is a childish, joking word for a fart.
fact: «Pìgu» means bottom or bum; it is a childish word, not a rude one.
exercise: Friends say «I had a brain fart.» What does it mean in this joke? | A loud noise from a drum | A kind of bean | *A silly mistake, said as a joke | A long walk in the rain
exercise: Which is the polite school word for letting wind out? | Toot, which is a rude word | *Pass wind | Fart around | Fart
exercise: Where does most fart gas come from? | A broken pipe in the house | Air from the sky only | Sugar from sweets | *Bacteria in the large gut breaking down fibre from food
test: «Old fart» means: | A very old car | A type of pudding | A kind grandad who tells stories | *A rude name for a boring or old-fashioned person
test: «Fart around» (UK) means: | To walk very slowly | To sing very loudly | *To waste time doing silly things | To cook a fast meal
exam: Which is the most polite word for passing wind? | Toot | Pìgu | Fart | *Pass wind
